---
title: Ultimate Nut Roast
description: Packed with flavour and boasts a wonderfully moist texture thanks to the chestnuts and lentils. The black garlic cloves add a deep umami flavour, balanced out by sweet bursts of dried cranberry.
image: https://media-cdn2.greatbritishchefs.com/media/fapbo2uq/img85189.whqc_1426x713q80.jpg
source: https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/recipes/nut-roast-recipe
tags: easy
course: Dinner
author: GBC Kitchen
servings: 8
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 45 minutes
---

Heat @butter{50%g} in a large #pan{} and sweat @onion{1}(diced), @leek{0.5}(sliced), @carrot{1}(cut into 5mm dice), and @garlic{3%clove}(finely sliced) until soft (about ~{10%minutes}). Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 180°C/gas mark 4.

Add @chestnut mushrooms{100%g}(chopped) and cook through, then add @black garlic{2%clove}(mashed to a paste), @puy lentils{100%g}(cooked), @chestnuts{180%g}(roughly chopped), @mixed nuts{100%g}(chopped), @dried cranberries{30%g}(or apricots, chopped), @brown bread{100%g}(torn into small pieces), and @vegetable stock{150%g}.

Leave to simmer until the stock is completely absorbed, then flavour the mixture with @orange{1}(zested), @nutmeg{}(to taste), @rosemary{1%tbsp}(finely chopped), @thyme{1%tbsp}(leaves), @salt{}, and @pepper{}.

Fold @eggs{2}(beaten) through the mixture then pack into a loaf tin lined with baking paper.

Place in the oven and cook for ~{35-45%minutes}, until browned and slightly crisp on the outside. Slice and serve immediately.
